WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:03.240
INTRO:
Do you know how Dubai makes their money?

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:08.920
The most common guess is likely oil, and given
that they’re surrounded by oil rich countries,

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.650
this is a fair guess, but it’s not actually
true.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:20.990
According to the CIA, 49.8% of Dubai’s GDP
comes from industry, 49.2% comes from services,

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:23.210
and 0.9% comes from agriculture.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:29.040
In other words, oil production accounts for
less than 1% of their GDP today.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.369
Meanwhile, Saudi Arabia is the exact opposite.

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:40.070
In Saudi Arabia, the petroleum sector accounts
for 42% of their GDP, 87% of their budget,

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:42.400
and 90% of their export earnings.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:47.210
And when you consider that their flagship
company, Saudi Aramco, often pulls in over

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:54.060
$100 billion in profit per year, their dependence
on oil hasn’t exactly been a problem.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:58.890
But, as the world slowly transitions over
to renewable energy, it’s not the best idea

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:03.130
to continue this dependence, and the Sauds
are well aware of this.

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:07.380
This is the main reason that they’ve been
investing so heavily into hospitality and

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:10.240
tourism over the past decade just like Dubai.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:16.030
For example, they spent $3.8 billion building
a phenomenal airport, they started handing

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:21.100
out tourist visas for the first time in 2019,
and most iconically, they’ve been trying

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:25.380
to dethrone the Burj Khalifa with their own
skyscraper called the Kingdom Tower.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:30.130
Yet, despite their efforts, none of these
plans have really led to much results.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:35.360
Their multi-billion dollar airport often looks
like this, and their kingdom tower which was

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.049
started construction in April of 2013 still
looks like this.

00:01:40.049 --> 00:01:44.369
Clearly, Saudi Arabia has had quite a bit
of trouble completing these attractions and

00:01:44.369 --> 00:01:45.760
attracting tourists.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:49.890
So, why is Saudi Arabia failing to copy Dubai?

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:57.090
POOR MARKETING:
By far, one of the biggest limiting factors

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:01.369
holding back Saudi Arabia is the negative
stigma surrounding the country.

00:02:01.369 --> 00:02:05.760
Whether it’s true or not, the western media
has painted an extremely negative picture

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.860
when it comes to Saudi Arabia.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:12.420
From women not even having simple rights like
driving or watching movies to gay people being

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:13.680
executed.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:18.180
Saudi Arabia has toned down a lot of their
stances and policies over the past several

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:22.939
years to become more open to tourists, but
the overall sentiment surrounding Saudi Arabia

00:02:22.939 --> 00:02:25.020
hasn’t really changed.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:28.959
According to tourists who have traveled to
Saudi Arabia, the common theme seems to be

00:02:28.959 --> 00:02:33.650
that if you’re respectful to their culture
and you don’t push the boundaries, you shouldn't

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:35.930
have any problems whatsoever.

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:40.150
With that being said though, when someone
is on vacation, they don’t necessarily want

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:42.709
to conform to guidelines like no drinking.

00:02:42.709 --> 00:02:47.340
So, Saudi Arabia naturally falls down their
list of vacation destinations.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:51.799
Something else to consider is that, people
don’t associate Saudi Arabia with vacation

00:02:51.799 --> 00:02:53.170
in the first place.

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:57.769
Dubai had to work decades to create this association,
and the primary way they accomplished this

00:02:57.769 --> 00:02:59.419
was through their airlines.

00:02:59.419 --> 00:03:04.230
We all know about the fancy middle eastern
airlines and their lavish first class residences,

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:08.199
but even the economy seating at these airlines
are the best in the world.

00:03:08.199 --> 00:03:12.760
And given that maximizing profit is not a
top priority for these airlines, they’re

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:17.389
able to offer extremely competitive rates
despite their superior experience.

00:03:17.389 --> 00:03:22.129
Over several years, as people traveled around
the world for work and vacation, they started

00:03:22.129 --> 00:03:26.219
to associate Emirates, Etihad, and Qatar Airways
with luxury.

00:03:26.219 --> 00:03:30.700
And naturally, this image carried over into
their respective countries and cities as well.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:36.230
If we’re being honest, no westerner would
know about Doha or Abu Dhabi if it wasn’t

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:41.749
for Qatar Airways and Etihad, so clearly these
airlines played a massive role in putting

00:03:41.749 --> 00:03:43.799
these cities on the global map.

00:03:43.799 --> 00:03:47.489
Saudi Arabia, however, doesn't have such an
airline.

00:03:47.489 --> 00:03:51.849
The average person likely doesn’t even know
what their airline is called or what the capital

00:03:51.849 --> 00:03:53.669
of Saudi Arabia is.

00:03:53.669 --> 00:03:58.459
And when you’re trying to become a tourist
destination, this is extremely bad news.

00:03:58.459 --> 00:04:03.099
Not only does the average person not associate
you with tourism, but they associate you with

00:04:03.099 --> 00:04:04.430
negative things.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:10.200
Now, this isn’t to say that Saudi Arabia
is bad and that Dubai is perfect because the

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:14.319
truth is, Dubai has a lot of the same shortfalls
as Saudi Arabia.

00:04:14.319 --> 00:04:18.810
For example, I’m sure we’ve all heard
about Saudi women trying to flee the country.

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:23.460
But, did you know that Princess Latifa, a
daughter of the ruler of Dubai, tried to flee

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:24.770
the UAE.

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:29.090
She accused her father of holding her quote
“hostage” and she was captured and taken

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:33.500
back to Dubai, so clearly, there’s something
going on there too.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:38.560
But, Dubai’s airline and hotel marketing
far outweigh such stories, and in the end,

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:41.190
that’s all it comes down to: marketing.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:47.010
Dubai has brilliant marketing while Saudi
Arabia does not, and as long as that doesn’t

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:51.920
change, Saudi Arabia will struggle to replicate
Dubai’s success.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:57.290
INTERNAL TURMOIL:
As we can see, Saudi Arabia is having a hard

00:04:57.290 --> 00:05:02.980
time with branding, but this shouldn’t stop
them from making internal progres right?

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:07.070
For example, successfully finishing the Kingdom
tower has nothing to do with how the world

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:08.850
views Saudi Arabia.

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:12.870
The success of this project solely depends
on factors that Saudi Arabia has control over

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:16.500
like budget, engineering talent, construction
workers, etc.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:22.280
Yet, Saudi Arabia is struggling in this sector
as well, so what went wrong?

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:27.820
Well, the answer is that while Saudi Arabia
has control over these factors, they haven’t

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:30.090
managed them particularly well.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:33.400
Starting with the budget, the Kingdom tower
was never really funded correctly.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:39.280
Originally, the tower was supposed to be 1
mile or 1600 meters tall.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:44.150
To put that in perspective, the Burj Khalifa
is only about half that size coming in at

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:45.600
829 meters.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:50.650
Given these sky high ambitions, the estimate
for the building was also sky high coming

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:54.280
in at $28.5 billion.

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:58.580
While Saudi Arabia initially approved this
plan, this proved to be too much even for

00:05:58.580 --> 00:05:59.580
them.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:05.160
They eventually reduced their blueprints to
a km high tower which was ok, but the problem

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:10.710
was that they also reduced the budget down
to $1.23 billion which is less than the Burj

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:13.490
Khalifa’s budget of $1.5 billion.

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:18.470
It’s not that this can’t be done, but
trying to accomplish an engineering feat and

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:22.460
a financial feat at the same time makes the
entire project magnitudes harder.

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:28.420
Aside from limited capital, the Kingdom tower
was also hammered by the 2017 Saudi Arabian

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:29.420
purge.

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:33.200
If y'all aren’t aware of this event, it
was basically when the crown prince of Saudi

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:38.480
Arabia, Mohammed Bin Salman, arrested the
most influential princes, ministers, and businessmen

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:41.690
in the country to apparently crack down on
corruption.

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:44.590
Now, these guys weren’t actually put in
jail.

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:49.000
Rather, they were put in a Ritz-Carlton Hotel
and they were barred from leaving until they

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:50.520
paid a hefty fine.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:55.100
And when I say hefty, I mean hundreds of millions
if not billions.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:07:00.990
By the end of the purge, Saudi Arabia recovered
a mind boggling $107 billion.

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:07.139
Clearly, the purge was extremely successful,
but the thing to note is that a lot of the

00:07:07.139 --> 00:07:11.330
businessmen who were arrested were the ones
that were responsible for building the Kingdom

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:12.540
Tower.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:18.360
Shortly after, in January of 2018, the construction
company would halt construction on the Kingdom

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:19.360
tower.

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:25.030
Now, the official reasoning is that this company
had labor issues with contractors, but honestly

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:27.979
I think it has more to do with the purge.

00:07:27.979 --> 00:07:33.639
I mean, if you milk these businessmen out
of $107 billion, it’s not crazy to think

00:07:33.639 --> 00:07:39.430
that they may be pissed off, and that they
might halt construction in retaliation.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:44.280
More recent news suggests that there has been
movement around the tower and that construction

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:45.280
has resumed.

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:48.840
But, the purge literally added half a decade
onto the project.

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:55.180
Here’s a side by side comparison of how
the tower looked in 2017 and 2022.

00:07:55.180 --> 00:07:58.850
Clearly, not much progress was made during
this timeframe.

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:03.240
And as the construction continues to drag
on, the primary question has transitioned

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:11.261
from whether Saudi Arabia can build the tower
to if they should build the tower.

00:08:11.261 --> 00:08:13.930
JUST WHY:
The concept of skyscrapers was born out of

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:15.250
necessity.

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:20.280
Cities with limited space couldn’t afford
to build horizontally, so they built vertically.

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:25.080
This gave construction companies a new challenge
as they tried to build the tallest, strongest,

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:27.530
and most practical towers in the world.

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:32.690
But, with mega projects like the Burj Khalifa,
the Shanghai Tower, the One World Trade Center,

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:37.060
and the Kingdom Tower, the most important
factor has completely disappeared from the

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:39.229
equation: practicality.

00:08:39.229 --> 00:08:42.099
Much of these buildings aren’t even occupiable.

00:08:42.099 --> 00:08:50.000
For example, 29% of the Burj Khalifa is unoccupiable
and 39% of the Burj Al Arab is unoccupiable.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:55.160
In contrast, less than 1% of the Empire State
Building is unoccupiable.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:09:00.620
Aside from wasting so much space, the space
that is used isn’t even used that efficiently.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:05.389
B1M recently posted a phenomenal video about
how the buildings on Billionaire’s Row are

00:09:05.389 --> 00:09:06.560
half empty.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:10.959
The billionaires who buy these properties
have little interest in actually living there.

00:09:10.959 --> 00:09:15.560
For them, it’s just a good place to park
some cash and it gives them some pride.

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:20.600
So, while these skyscrapers are insane feats
of engineering, they serve very little value

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:23.779
to society, and countries are starting to
take notice.

00:09:23.779 --> 00:09:28.699
China, for example, is cracking down on what
they deem vanity projects.

00:09:28.699 --> 00:09:33.209
Considering this, the question becomes, is
the Kingdom Tower even worth it for Saudi

00:09:33.209 --> 00:09:34.209
Arabia?

00:09:34.209 --> 00:09:36.889
Let’s say everything goes perfectly for
Saudi Arabia.

00:09:36.889 --> 00:09:40.999
Let’s say they’re able to rebrand themselves
and that they finish the tower?

00:09:40.999 --> 00:09:43.059
Will tourists just start flooding in?

00:09:43.059 --> 00:09:45.930
Well, I think the answer is not really.

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:51.850
I mean that’s exactly what Doha did, and
how many more people go to Dubai vs Doha.

00:09:51.850 --> 00:09:56.959
The truth is, Dubai was the city that invented
the desert kingdom image, and unless they

00:09:56.959 --> 00:10:01.089
screw up really badly, they’re always going
to be tourist’s top choice.

00:10:01.089 --> 00:10:04.949
Simply building a taller tower or a larger
airport isn’t going to take that title away

00:10:04.949 --> 00:10:05.980
from Dubai.

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:10.290
Not to mention, Dubai is building something
called the Creek Tower which is supposed to

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:11.790
beat out the Kingdom Tower.

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:16.790
So, it’s not clear how long Saudi Arabia
could even hold onto the title of having the

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:18.319
world’s tallest tower.

00:10:18.319 --> 00:10:24.490
In other words, Saudi Arabia can’t just
build their way into replacing Dubai.

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:29.279
SOLUTION:
At the end of the day, to really understand

00:10:29.279 --> 00:10:33.689
why Saudi Arabia is struggling to emulate
Dubai’s success, we have to think about

00:10:33.689 --> 00:10:36.420
why people even travel in the first place.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:41.149
They travel to experience something new and
unique and to relax and have fun.

00:10:41.149 --> 00:10:46.220
If Riyadh is just a copy of Dubai, what’s
new or unique about it?

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:50.100
Also, you don’t have to have crazy architecture
to attract loads of tourists.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:54.869
In fact, most tourist destinations don’t
have the architecture or luxury that Dubai

00:10:54.869 --> 00:10:58.560
does, yet they remain extremely attractive
destinations.

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:02.649
Take Tokyo, for example, their skyline isn’t
anything particularly remarkable.

00:11:02.649 --> 00:11:06.990
But, it’s one of the most popular travel
destinations thanks to its rich culture and

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:08.010
food.

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:10.589
Similarly, why do people go to Singapore?

00:11:10.589 --> 00:11:16.100
It’s not because they have crazy buildings,
it’s once again because of culture and food,

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:20.589
and I’m not sure why Saudi Arabia doesn’t
embrace these aspects more.

00:11:20.589 --> 00:11:24.709
Saudi Arabia is literally the center of Islamic
culture and heritage.

00:11:24.709 --> 00:11:30.110
Now, I’m not suggesting opening up Mecca
to the public, but there’s so many historical

00:11:30.110 --> 00:11:33.660
monuments and mosques that you can’t find
anywhere else.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:38.220
Why not embrace what no one else has instead
of trying to become a soulless lavish place

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:39.680
like Dubai?

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:43.269
This isn’t to say that Saudi Arabia should
abandon the Kingdom Tower.

00:11:43.269 --> 00:11:48.259
I know this falls under the sunk cost fallacy,
but they’ve already spent so many resources

00:11:48.259 --> 00:11:52.050
and so much effort on this tower that they
might as well finish it.

00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:56.689
With that being said though, I don’t think
they should start any other vanity projects.

00:11:56.689 --> 00:12:01.860
Instead, I think the bulk of their efforts
should go into embracing what makes them unique.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:07.120
After all, 2.5 million pilgrims already travel
to Saudi Arabia every year.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:11.689
Why not embrace their culture and make this
tens of millions, but that’s just what I

00:12:11.689 --> 00:12:12.689
think.

00:12:12.689 --> 00:12:14.689
Would you guys ever travel to Saudi Arabia?

00:12:14.689 --> 00:12:15.949
Comment that down below.

00:12:15.949 --> 00:12:20.769
Also, drop a like if you agree that copying
Dubai is not the way to go.

